# T3. A blocked gripper doesn't stall the timeline. The skill closes its gripper to 4°, but the object stops it at
# 12°. After the skill's grasp event the gripper is exempt from divergence and the stall and load rules (the
# contract's), at 30% torque, and the skill's clock runs on: it ends on time (4.5 s, well before its 7.6 s
# deadline), holding, and the Pi asks "Let go?". It is offered by id only (the SIMULATED offer source), worded
# from the skill file's own title.
expect motion mode ready
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key pose-ready-left
wait 2100
key c
expect 5000 motion command arm.go_to_pose completed operator_cli
key object-left
key offer-skill-sample
expect motion target skill.run offer: SIMULATED sample: hold it out
expect spoke SIMULATED sample: hold it out. Park the walker and lock the brakes, then press Confirm.
wait 2100
key c
expect 6000 motion command skill.run completed offer
absent 10 motion fault
expect motion target gripper.release walker_local: Let go?
key inspect-grip-left
expect sim left gripper goal-present=-5
key inspect-left
expect sim limit=600,600,600,600,600,300
# Still holding while the walker asks: no fault in the next 2 s.
absent 2000 motion fault
key q
